Description: vfs_busy_try() makes a mount busy without waiting
 vfs_busy() with LK_NOWAIT returns at once for a mount that is being
 unmounted, but waits for the mount's lock while an update holds it. ZFS
 makes a mount busy while it holds locks that a remount waits for, so it
 needs a form that never waits. vfs_busy_try() returns EBUSY when the
 lock is held exclusively and ENOENT when the mount is being unmounted.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: no
